      "id": 1,
      "text": "The High Bridge Ranger Station, built in 1933\u201134 by the Civilian Conservation Corps, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/places/high-bridge.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The ranger station was constructed by the U.S. Forest Service, preserving the historic character of the Stehekin Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/places/high-bridge.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "High Bridge marks the point where Lake Chelan National Recreation Area ends and North Cascades National Park begins.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/places/high-bridge.htm",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "From the bridge you can see the rushing Stehekin River, a dramatic backdrop that draws hikers and photographers alike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.nps.gov/places/high-bridge.htm",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "High Bridge sits 11 miles up Stehekin Valley Road from Stehekin Landing, a remote gateway to the North Cascades.",
